f <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isma%27ilism\" target=\"_blank\">Ismaili</a> history, by an anonymous author&quot;\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T16:18:00-08:00","id":1501494,"title":"","content":"<b>B\u0101\u1e6din</b> or <b>baten</b> (<a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arabic_language\" target=\"_blank\">Arabic</a>: \u0628\u0627\u0637\u0646) literally means &quot;inner&quot;, &quot;inward&quot;, &quot;hidden&quot;, etc. The <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quran\" target=\"_blank\">Quran</a>, for instance, has a hidden meaning in contrast to its exterior or apparent meaning, the <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zahir_(Islam)\" target=\"_blank\">zahir</a> (zaher). <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sufism\" target=\"_blank\">Sufis</a> believe that every individual has a batin in the world of souls. It is the inward self of the individual; when cleansed with the light of one's spiritual guide, it elevates a person spiritually. This notion is connected to <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allah\" target=\"_blank\">Allah</a>'s attribute of the Hidden One, who cannot be seen but exists in every realm.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T16:18:52-08:00","id":1501495,"title":"","content":"Many <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isma%27ilism\" target=\"_blank\">Ismaili</a> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muslims\" target=\"_blank\">Muslim</a> thinkers have stressed the importance of the balance between the exoteric (<i><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zahir_(Islam)\" target=\"_blank\">zahir</a></i>) and the esoteric (<i>batin</i>) in the understanding of faith, and have explained that spiritual interpretation (<a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Esoteric_interpretation_of_the_Quran\" target=\"_blank\"><i>ta\u2019wil</i></a>) entails elucidating the esoteric meaning (<i>b\u0101tin</i>) from the exoteric form (<i><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zahir_(Islam)\" target=\"_blank\">zahir</a></i>).<br /> <br /> Muslim groups believe that <i>batin </i>can be fully understood only by a figure with esoteric knowledge. For <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shia_Islam\" target=\"_blank\">Shia Muslims</a>, that is the <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imamah_(Shi%27a_doctrine)\" target=\"_blank\">Imam of Time</a>.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T16:19:22-08:00","id":1501496,"title":"","content":"In a wider sense, batin is the inner meaning or reality behind all existence, the <i>zahir</i> being the world of form and the apparent meaning.<br /> <br /> A grounding feature of <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isma%27ilism\" target=\"_blank\">Ismailism</a> is the co-existence of the physical and the spiritual, the <i>zahir</i> (exoteric) form and the <i>batin</i> (esoteric) essence. The esoteric is the source of the exoteric, and the exoteric is the manifestation of the esoteric. This concept is highlighted in the \u201cEpistle of the Right Path\u201d, a <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persian_language\" target=\"_blank\">Persian</a> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isma%27ilism\" target=\"_blank\">Ismaili</a> prose text from the post-Mongol period of <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isma%27ilism\" target=\"_blank\">Ismaili</a> history, by an anonymous author&quot;\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T16:29:27-08:00","id":1501498,"title":"","content":"The texts above were taken from Wikipedia from the meaning of the world &quot;Batin&quot;. Bellow is my own personal take on it:<br /> <br /> <i>Ahl I</i> literally translates as &quot;The people of&quot;<br /> <br /> Therefore, <i>Ahl-I-Batin </i>would be something like &quot;The People of The Occult (or Inner) Knownledge&quot;, or the ones that see the &quot;hidden world&quot;. It clearly implies a concept that bears ressemblence to the traditions ideas of &quot;Avatars&quot; and &quot;Ascension&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1501480#post1501480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably for the best that the early writeups did not go too in depth with the Batini. Given how often mages end up being the ones who know the true meaning of Christianity/Buddhism/etc, they probably would have been quite offensive. As it is, despite being one of the main Islamic factions they predate Islam.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we are to take on the literal ipsis literu name of the tradition, <i>Ahl-I-Batin, </i>or &quot;the people with hidden/esoteric knowledge&quot; (or &quot;the people with TRUE knowledge&quot; if you were to interpret it), than it is already too late for that, because it already implies that they are the real deal of the islamic doctrine.<br /> <br /> What's even worse, while &quot;Celestial Chorus&quot; means jack shit for real world christian doctrine, Bateen (or Batin) is a real life esoteric view present in real life islamic mysticism, so it is not just some cool sounding name just for the gags like &quot;Virtual Adepts&quot; or &quot;Dreamspeakers&quot;. The only other group that does that is the Order of Hermes who is the real name of a real group of occultism research, but it's so fringe that nobody cares.<br /> <br /> But that wouldnt be very diffe5 from naming a Tradition something like &quot;Children of the Holy Baptism&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T17:50:42-08:00","id":1501583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1501498#post1501498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The texts above were taken from Wikipedia from the meaning of the world &quot;Batin&quot;. Bellow is my own personal take on it:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would be wary when using Wikipedia. Anybody can go in and write/edit anything they want, when they want. You would probably get more accurate information from Muslim scholars than from Wikipedia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 01-28-2023, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T10:28:58-08:00","id":1501624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1501583#post1501583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would be wary when using Wikipedia. Anybody can go in and write/edit anything they want, when they want. You would probably get more accurate information from Muslim scholars than from Wikipedia.</div> </div> </div> </div>The information about the meaning of the word is accurate, I just used Wikipedia for the easyness to understand the information, in a format easier to digest, instead of a long theological dissertation.<br /> <br /> It was just to give an idea about the meaning, not going into a lenght study over it. I personally know quite a bit about islam - Im not scholar, but Im well informed. I am well aware about how untrustworthy Wikipedia is, but in this case the information is accurate, and enough for its purposes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T06:39:53-08:00","id":1501696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1501498#post1501498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are to take on the literal ipsis literu name of the tradition, <i>Ahl-I-Batin, </i>or &quot;the people with hidden/esoteric knowledge&quot; (or &quot;the people with TRUE knowledge&quot; if you were to interpret it), than it is already too late for that, because it already implies that they are the real deal of the islamic doctrine.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly tricky territory, but a Mage group that claims hidden or mystical knowledge of a real world religion is not inherently a problem. Lots of religions recognize some form of deeper or mystical understanding that ordinary practitioners just don't have. A key element of this is that this hidden understanding does not contradict the major tenets of the faith. By the same reasoning we can have mage factions based on hidden or mystical understanding of a religion, but if we want them to be at all representative of that religion their mystical understanding can't contradict mainstream practice and beliefs.<br /> <br /> Staying vague about what the hidden knowledge is or limiting it to well known mystical understandings would be the safest path. I don't know enough about Islam to say for sure if the Batini writups cross the line or not, but given how other Traditions have been handled I'm fairly certain they would have crossed that line severely if they had had more definition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's even worse, while &quot;Celestial Chorus&quot; means jack shit for real world christian doctrine, Bateen (or Batin) is a real life esoteric view present in real life islamic mysticism, so it is not just some cool sounding name just for the gags like &quot;Virtual Adepts&quot; or &quot;Dreamspeakers&quot;. The only other group that does that is the Order of Hermes who is the real name of a real group of occultism research, but it's so fringe that nobody cares.<br /> <br /> But that wouldnt be very diffe5 from naming a Tradition something like &quot;Children of the Holy Baptism&quot;. </div> </div> </div>While the name has no real meaning, the Chorus is still put forward as the predominant Tradition for Christians, Jews, and Muslims, and its tenets and history are wildly incompatible with the mainstream beliefs of all three. A name is only one part of the identity of a Tradition. <br /> <br /> Edit: The name &quot;Ahl-I-Batin&quot; is enough to show that the faction is Arabic in origin and heavily implies they are Islamic (so much so that while it technically works if they aren't connected, it really shouldn't be their name). Whether it is an offensive use of the name depends heavily on the beliefs of the faction and how well they mesh with mainstream Islam. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 01-30-2023, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T09:08:34-08:00","id":1501715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1501696#post1501696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's certainly tricky territory, but a Mage group that claims hidden or mystical knowledge of a real world religion is not inherently a problem. Lots of religions recognize some form of deeper or mystical understanding that ordinary practitioners just don't have. A key element of this is that this hidden understanding does not contradict the major tenets of the faith. By the same reasoning we can have mage factions based on hidden or mystical understanding of a religion, but if we want them to be at all representative of that religion their mystical understanding can't contradict mainstream practice and beliefs.<br /> <br /> Staying vague about what the hidden knowledge is or limiting it to well known mystical understandings would be the safest path. I don't know enough about Islam to say for sure if the Batini writups cross the line or not, but given how other Traditions have been handled I'm fairly certain they would have crossed that line severely if they had had more definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, absolutely. Islam have a strong monotheistic doctrine, even more so than Christianism itself, on par with judaism, so all the vague assertions about &quot;Unity&quot; for the Ahl-I-Batin dont strand too far off. And like exemplified by the very concept of Batin, or &quot;hidden world&quot;, islamic mysticism has this idea that there is more beyond than just what is perceived by the eyes in the material world, and that's also close to some ideas in the MtA (like being a &quot;Sleeper&quot; who takes the world at face value, or an &quot;Awakened&quot;, who sees the hidden world).<br /> <br /> Islamic mysticism however is NOT the mainstream - just like Christian or Jewish mysticism aint either.<br /> <br /> But I absolutely agree that, if the writters tried to delve too deep into fully fleshing out the Batini, it would quickly devolve into a giant mess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [quote]While the name has no real meaning, the Chorus is still put forward as the predominant Tradition for Christians, Jews, and Muslims, and its tenets and history are wildly incompatible with the mainstream beliefs of all three. A name is only one part of the identity of a Tradition.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, I agree 100%, I was just pointing out to the name, in terms of practices the Chorus is an absolutely nonsensical mess, no doubt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: The name &quot;Ahl-I-Batin&quot; is enough to show that the faction is Arabic in origin and heavily implies they are Islamic (so much so that while it technically works if they aren't connected, it really shouldn't be their name). Whether it is an offensive use of the name depends heavily on the beliefs of the faction and how well they mesh with mainstream Islam.<br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div>I dont think the name is offensive at all, it's just a name that indicates &quot;we are students of the occult with Allah as our guide&quot;. It holds no derrogatory conotation, my line of reasoning was just to say that there is a clear link between the name and islamic theological study, but no much more can said about it. Much like &quot;Children of Baptism&quot; would indicate a clear christian link, but that wouldnt be derrogatory either. <br /> <br /> What would be offensive would be if they were thoroughly described and held a bunch of haram (haram: sinful) practices and ideas - which is what would probably happen, particularly in a game world of witches and pagan Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T11:18:15-08:00","id":1501726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1501715#post1501715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yes, absolutely. Islam have a strong monotheistic doctrine, even more so than Christianism itself, on par with judaism, so all the vague assertions about &quot;Unity&quot; for the Ahl-I-Batin dont strand too far off. And like exemplified by the very concept of Batin, or &quot;hidden world&quot;, islamic mysticism has this idea that there is more beyond than just what is perceived by the eyes in the material world, and that's also close to some ideas in the MtA (like being a &quot;Sleeper&quot; who takes the world at face value, or an &quot;Awakened&quot;, who sees the hidden world).<br /> <br /> Islamic mysticism however is NOT the mainstream - just like Christian or Jewish mysticism aint either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not mainstream is not the same thing as heretical, though. As you say, Christian mysticism is not mainstream, yet there are quite a few mystics among the saints of the Catholic and Orthodox denominations. What they said and the devotions they left behind definitely go beyond the necessary doctrines of the churches, yet none of them contradict those doctrines. If they did, they wouldn't be saints. <br /> <br /> A representative faction doesn't have to be mainstream, it just can't contradict the orthodoxy. They can, and perhaps even should, claim a deeper understanding of their religions but never mutually exclusive one (which is where Mage has misstepped in the past). <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T05:50:31-08:00","id":1501805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1501726#post1501726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not mainstream is not the same thing as heretical, though. As you say, Christian mysticism is not mainstream, yet there are quite a few mystics among the saints of the Catholic and Orthodox denominations. What they said and the devotions they left behind definitely go beyond the necessary doctrines of the churches, yet none of them contradict those doctrines. If they did, they wouldn't be saints.<br /> <br /> A representative faction doesn't have to be mainstream, it just can't contradict the orthodoxy. They can, and perhaps even should, claim a deeper understanding of their religions but never mutually exclusive one (which is where Mage has misstepped in the past).</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point. Yes, I completely agree. I think that indeed, any deeper characterization of the Batini would have to take that aspect into consideration, otherwise it would incur the risk of running into the Celestial Chorus, which aint truly representative of anything in the real world - actually, the Chorus could function as an order of freemasons, their ideologies are somewhat similar, which is why they accept anyone in their ranks, but most are christians, with some jews and even muslims. And I say this because I myself was one, and I had jews and muslim brothers in the order. So, the freemasons would actually be the closest to the Chorus in real life, but... They dont seem to have been molded after that in the game, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T07:19:53-08:00","id":1501812,"title":"","content":"No, they aren't. As Ramnesis has pointed out elsewhere, they're basically a retroactive version of Theosophy with primarily Christian symbolism layered on top.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T19:12:16-08:00","id":1501911,"title":"","content":"Might I suggest simply having the Batini use an alternate Sphere, a la &quot;Data&quot; or &quot;Dimensional Science&quot;? Call it &quot;Fate&quot; and have it be worse at stereotypically 'evil' applications of Entropy, and better at things like predictions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26077,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26077-chaotic-nipple","user":"Chaotic-nipple","date":". 02-01-2023, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26077-chaotic-nipple","name":"Chaotic-nipple","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T17:39:15-08:00","id":1501992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1501480#post1501480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably for the best that the early writeups did not go too in depth with the Batini. Given how often mages end up being the ones who know the true meaning of Christianity/Buddhism/etc, they probably would have been quite offensive. As it is, despite being one of the main Islamic factions they predate Islam.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the &quot;we know what is <i>really</i> going on&quot; aspect is a natural outgrowth of the Awakened understanding certain underpinnings of reality (or at least believing they understand it) combined with the game's themes of hubris (it's not the only theme, but it is one of them). Mages are all just a bit full of themselves to one degree or another, and naturally think they understand their own cultures or undertakings better than any of &quot;The Masses&quot;. Not that they should necessarily be right though. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T20:20:23-08:00","id":1501999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1501812#post1501812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they aren't. As Ramnesis has pointed out elsewhere, they're basically a retroactive version of Theosophy with primarily Christian symbolism layered on top.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have always found that the Chorus seem to make more sense if you look at them as essentially Gnostic* heretics who pretend to be practitioners of other monotheistic and quasi-monotheistic faiths, and use those real world faiths as &quot;gateways&quot; to The One the same way the Akashics use real world fighting styles and philosophies as gateways to Do. But that's just me. <br /> <br /> *(Not literal real world historical Gnostics, but the same basic concept of having secret knowledge and truths only available to the properly initiated.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T06:33:07-08:00","id":1502021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1501999#post1501999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have always found that the Chorus seem to make more sense if you look at them as essentially Gnostic* heretics who pretend to be practitioners of other monotheistic and quasi-monotheistic faiths, and use those real world faiths as &quot;gateways&quot; to The One the same way the Akashics use real world fighting styles and philosophies as gateways to Do. But that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Incidentally, the Akashic Brotherhood is another Tradition with some obvious Theosophical origins. The Akashic Record, for instance, is a concept directly from Theosophy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T16:23:34-08:00","id":1502255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1501812#post1501812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they aren't. As Ramnesis has pointed out elsewhere, they're basically a retroactive version of Theosophy with primarily Christian symbolism layered on top.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blergh that makes me like them even less","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T16:25:52-08:00","id":1502256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaotic-nipple</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1501911#post1501911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might I suggest simply having the Batini use an alternate Sphere, a la &quot;Data&quot; or &quot;Dimensional Science&quot;? Call it &quot;Fate&quot; and have it be worse at stereotypically 'evil' applications of Entropy, and better at things like predictions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like that<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1501992#post1501992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the &quot;we know what is <i>really</i> going on&quot; aspect is a natural outgrowth of the Awakened understanding certain underpinnings of reality (or at least believing they understand it) combined with the game's themes of hubris (it's not the only theme, but it is one of them). Mages are all just a bit full of themselves to one degree or another, and naturally think they understand their own cultures or undertakings better than any of &quot;The Masses&quot;. Not that they should necessarily be right though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that this says: &quot;Christianism? Pfff. Bollocks. We know the true truth, and the truth is Theosophy&quot;.<br /> <br /> It negates real world faiths. I mean, I personally have no problems whatsoever with this, but I dont have any personal faith.<br /> <br /> It is also a bit hypocritical, since everybody is always very careful not to insult muslims, but the same care is not given to christians, nor to other religions like buddhism or hinduism (I mean, the Eutanatoi and Akashics are grotesque misrepresentations of two massive cultural groups related to those)\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 02-05-2023, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T17:00:52-08:00","id":1502259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1502256#post1502256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually like that</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that Dark Ages: Mage have the Batini the Pillars (\u201cUbaddan\u201d) of fate (\u201cal-Anbiya\u201d), minds (\u201cal-Fatihah\u201d), space (\u201cal-Hajj\u201d), and secrecy (\u201cal-Layl\u201d). Al-Hajj is basically Correspondence; I could see using al-Ajbiya as a guideline when decision an alternate Sphere of Fate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1502256#post1502256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that this says: &quot;Christianism? Pfff. Bollocks. We know the true truth, and the truth is Theosophy&quot;.<br /> <br /> It negates real world faiths. I mean, I personally have no problems whatsoever with this, but I dont have any personal faith.<br /> <br /> It is also a bit hypocritical, since everybody is always very careful not to insult muslims, but the same care is not given to christians, nor to other religions like buddhism or hinduism (I mean, the Eutanatoi and Akashics are grotesque misrepresentations of two massive cultural groups related to those)\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I would recommend that we review <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>' <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1493716-alternative-traditions-origins\"> Alternative Traditions Origins</a> thread. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T14:46:02-08:00","id":1503067,"title":"","content":"As far as I'm concerned, the Batini prohibition against Entropy only works if you mono-focus on Entropy as a Sphere of endings, decay, and chaos. It wouldn't be a problem if you called it &quot;Fortune&quot;, as was done in Mage: The Sorcerer's Crusade. (And, lo and behold, Batini have no trouble using Fortune in that version of Mage.)<br /> <br /> The ideal way of handling it would instead be to have Batini use Entropy just fine, but be limited in what applications they can use it for. Hardly a new phenomenon among mages. It's common for Mage factions to use some parts of a Sphere but not others. No matter their mastery of Life, a New World Order operative won't be shapeshifting into animals anytime soon (at least not of their own will). Nor will a Verbana witch use Forces to blast people with radiation.<br /> <br /> A Batini mage could easily use Entropy's fate or luck manipulating aspects. Justifying it as smoothing over the illusions of the world, and bringing events into concordance with what the mage believes to be the eventual (positive, holistic) outcome. But they'd never be able to use it to rot someone from the inside out. Both because it defies the belief in a non-dualistic, &quot;all is one&quot; reality where endings are an illusion, and also because they'd see it as repugnant. I can also see the Batini manipulating events to ensure they go unseen through happenstance, supplementing their Arcane. Or to cut through deception and determine the truth in someone's words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T17:15:13-08:00","id":1503281,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> This seems like a very sensible approach to this and one I'd suggest to any players questioning the entropy thing in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-16T02:57:12-07:00","id":1553851,"title":"","content":"I would like to go back to what was said earlier because there is an error regarding the Muslim doctrine. Indeed, it was stated in the very first message that &quot;God is all of creation,&quot; and this is contrary to the concept of <i>Tawhid</i>. In Islam, the doctrine teaches that the Creator is infinitely above His creation and that He is external to it. This is why we say that He is the Most High.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28917-yahya","name":"Yahya","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-16T19:22:55-07:00","id":1553865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yahya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1553851#post1553851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to go back to what was said earlier because there is an error regarding the Muslim doctrine. Indeed, it was stated in the very first message that &quot;God is all of creation,&quot; and this is contrary to the concept of <i>Tawhid</i>. In Islam, the doctrine teaches that the Creator is infinitely above His creation and that He is external to it. This is why we say that He is the Most High.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not exactly an error, the point is the following bit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heilong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin#post1501266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Some disclaimers:</i><br /> The ideas are typically from non-mainstream, non-orthodox Islamic teachings.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>What happens is that the Ahl-i-Batin are heavily based on Sufi mysticism, and their <i>Doctrine of Unity</i> is then based on the Sufi idea of <i>Wahdat Al-Wujud</i> (<i>Unity of Existence</i>) as expressed by Ibn Arabi.<br /> <br /> You are right that this isn't by any stretch how most Muslims read <i>tawhid</i>, and I think this should have been made clearer. I'm not even sure if this interpretation is common among Sufis, or was how Ibn Arabi really understood <i>Wahdat Al-Wujud</i>\u200b.<br /> <br /> But in the end this is the pattern the game follows on everything. Every Tradition is superficially based on a larger cultural &quot;thing&quot;, but actually focused on a very specific mystical movement within that group that breaks with a lot of their orthodox thought. The Batini at least are based on a movement with more than millennium of history and well regarded by many Muslims, the standard MtA approach is to get some 19th century British or American mystical shenanigan and pseudo-historicize it by making it the secret core of their magical traditions.<br /> <br /> I can't even say for sure if this is a bad approach, although it surely should have more disclaimers. We have to keep in mind that those Traditions are game elements, they're not meant to be accurate descriptions of cultures or religions. Even within the fiction of the setting they're not how normal people do things, they're about Mages, and Mages in the game are monsters with the power to break reality and force it into conforming to their views, so they're by definition barred from ever truly knowing the truth about anything, or even truly deferring to the wisdom of others.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-17T02:33:05-07:00","id":1553869,"title":"","content":"Yes, indeed, there is a sectarian current that believes that Allah is present everywhere in creation, and as you mentioned, this belief is called <i>Wahdat Al-Wujud</i>. I had intentionally not brought up this point because I did not want to confuse the reader with concepts that are too complex and marginal within Islam. I only wished to present <a href=\"https://www.lesjoyauxdarabie.com/cp/tawhid/\" target=\"_blank\">the Sunni doctrine</a><a href=\"https://www.lesjoyauxdarabie.com/cp/tawhid/\" target=\"_blank\"> of Monotheism </a>as it is primarily known within the Muslim community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28917-yahya","user":"Yahya","date":". 09-22-2025, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28917-yahya","name":"Yahya","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-17T09:14:24-07:00","id":1553874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yahya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1553869#post1553869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, indeed, there is a sectarian current that believes that Allah is present everywhere in creation, and as you mentioned, this belief is called <i>Wahdat Al-Wujud</i>. I had intentionally not brought up this point because I did not want to confuse the reader with concepts that are too complex and marginal within Islam. I only wished to present the Sunni doctrine as it is primarily known within the Muslim community.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which is the reason I think it's on them not making adequate disclaimers. A lot of readers make that exactly mistake of thinking the Batini are based on mainstream Muslim concepts.<br /> <br /> But being based on <i>Wahdat Al-Wujud</i> was actually their point. Maybe they should have just named it like that instead of calling <i>Doctrine of Unity</i>, it would at least make their intentions clearer to anyone who knows or researches Islam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T07:47:05-07:00","id":1553899,"title":"","content":"This is something we've run into on other threads. While it makes sense that there would be a significant faction of Sufi mages, it requires a significant suspension of disbelief to accept that there's no major faction of Sunni mages. <br /> <br /> Possibly... just possibly... they might be in the Celestial Chorus out of necessity (it's unlikely to be for any other reason). I'd have to check older books. The M20 CC section only mentions Isma'ili Islam and the Bektashi Order, which I understand are Shia and Sufi respectively? Meanwhile the wiki for the CC only mentions a small order of Sufi mages and says that at least within the middle east most Muslim mages end up with the Ahl-i-Batin.<br /> <br /> Though you should always take the mage wikis with a grain of salt, there's some nonsensical stuff in there.<br /> '<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T10:09:39-07:00","id":1553901,"title":"","content":"To be honest, how many Mages that follow any major religion at all would be really happy with any of the Traditions? They're all based on fairly minor offshoots, modern mysticism, unorthodox teachings, or crude generalizations. At best they work because need trumps belief. The best take you can get is maybe that Mages flock to those beliefs because they're Mages, not normal people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T10:59:06-07:00","id":1553905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1553901#post1553901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, how many Mages that follow any major religion at all would be really happy with any of the Traditions? They're all based on fairly minor offshoots, modern mysticism, unorthodox teachings, or crude generalizations. At best they work because need trumps belief. The best take you can get is maybe that Mages flock to those beliefs because they're Mages, not normal people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very few indeed. As you pointed out earlier the Ahl-i-Batin are notable in that they are actually based on a real and recognized form of Islam. Most major religions don't even get that. <br /> <br /> Niche occult societies vs para-governmental conspiracies is a fun concept, but setting that up in a believable and non-offensive way is much harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T03:51:34-07:00","id":1558985,"title":"","content":"You can follow a discussion on the topic by following this link <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin/page3\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...-i-batin/page3</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28917-yahya","name":"Yahya","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T06:39:01-07:00","id":1558989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yahya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1558985#post1558985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can follow a discussion on the topic by following this link <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin/page3\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...-i-batin/page3</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a link to this thread. I think you meant to post this in another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-30T08:20:48-07:00","id":1559120,"title":"","content":"Hello all, nice to see this post getting some attention. I read some of the folliw up posts and changed &quot;tawid&quot; to &quot;<i>Wahdat Al-Wujud</i>&quot; as recommended. Appreciate the community providing clarity on that.<br /> my goal in the original post was to share ideas on this Mage faction and hopefully get some feedback on the concepts behind them. Without background context, the Batini made zero sense to me and seemed to be randomly unrelated ideas mashed together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12269-heilong","name":"Heilong","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}